mbrotli
=======

This crate is a Rust port of the Brotli reference encoder from
https://github.com/google/brotli (v1.2.0, commit 028fb5a).

Portions of this software — including the static dictionary data, the transform
tables, the prefix-code tables, the context-mode lookup tables and the encoder
algorithms they belong to — are derived from that work, which is distributed
under the MIT license reproduced below. The upstream license text is also
vendored verbatim at `brotli-ffi/vendor/brotli/LICENSE`.

The native Rust decoder shares those format tables and dictionary bytes under
`src/shared/`. Its independently structured state machines follow RFC 7932 and
RFC 9841, with Google Brotli 1.2.0 used as a format reference and test oracle.
The borrowed word transformation implementation serves both codecs. The
upstream compressed regression fixtures retain the same Brotli Authors license.

